-- The main story of Polished Crystal 3.2.3 as steps a robot can follow
-- (female player, Chikorita), traced from the v3.2.3 scripts.
--
-- Steps are in playing order. The chapters are the 13 checkpoints of
-- story_presets.lua, in the same order (C10_TOWER before C09_RISING), with
-- the same route and choices: the steps of a chapter, played from that
-- chapter's starting save, should give that checkpoint's changes.
-- check_steps.py re-checks names, coordinates and source lines, and with
-- --presets compares each chapter with its checkpoint.
--
-- Every step has:
--   id          "S0001", ... in playing order
--   checkpoint  the chapter (checkpoint id) it belongs to
--   title       a few words
--   kind        one of:
--     go      reach `map`, or the spot `x`,`y` on it (the robot finds its way)
--     talk    press A facing the person at `target_x`,`target_y` (its
--             object_event coordinates), whose sprite is `sprite`
--     read    press A facing the bg_event at `target_x`,`target_y`
--     step    walk onto the coord_event tile `x`,`y`
--     answer  the choice at a yes/no box or menu: `choice` ("YES", "NO",
--             a menu entry, or "DEFAULT_NAME" at name entry); `prompt`
--             says which question
--     battle  win it: a trainer (`trainer` = class constant, `trainer_id`
--             = id as the script loads it) or a wild/scripted Pokemon
--             (`wild` = species, `level`; `catch = true` to catch it).
--             Optional `target_x`,`target_y` = the trainer's object_event.
--     use     use a field move or item (`use` = "CUT", "SURF", "STRENGTH",
--             "SQUIRTBOTTLE", "CARD_KEY", ...) facing `target_x`,`target_y`
--             "POKE_FLUTE_RADIO" wakes a Snorlax: Polished has no flute
--             item; tune the Pokegear radio to the Poke Flute station
--             (`radio_knob` = the tuner position), then press A facing it.
--     wait    a scene that plays by itself
--   Optional on any step: `facing` = the direction the player must face
--   ("UP", "DOWN", "LEFT", "RIGHT") when it matters, and `now_x`,`now_y`
--   = where a moving person stands at that moment (e.g. the Ilex Forest
--   Farfetch'd), when it isn't at its object_event spot any more.
--   map         the map the step happens on (map constant)
--   expect      what the scripts say changes by the end of the step:
--               events_set / events_clear, engine_set / engine_clear,
--               scenes { map, scene }, items { NAME, count }, key_items,
--               tms_hms, taken { NAME, count }, pokemon { SPECIES, level },
--               phone, and `map` = the map the player is on afterwards
--   sources     "file:line" in the v3.2.3 source for the step's script
--   unsure      guesses
--
-- Coordinates are the same as in the .asm event macros. Flags changed by
-- appear/disappear are the object's event flag (cited at its object_event).
-- Travel is on foot and by Surf: the main path never gets Fly.

return {
