  -- C09_RISING (95 steps)
  -- note: Route and choices follow presets/C09_RISING_notes.md, on foot (no
  -- Fly): Goldenrod -> Mahogany -> Route 44 -> Ice Path (HM Waterfall ball,
  -- B1F boulders 1-4) -> Blackthorn -> Gym (boulders 1 and 3, Clair) ->
  -- Dragon's Den -> Dragon Shrine quiz (badge) -> TM Dragon Pulse at (19,30)
  -- -> Blackthorn Pokemon Center.
  -- note: FORCED TRAINERS: the earlier trace only checked physical blocking. I
  -- re-checked every map on the route with a sight-line path search (collision
  -- rendered from the .ablk + tileset collision, ice sliding, ledges, side
  -- walls; a trainer sees `range` tiles straight ahead; spinning trainers
  -- treated as avoidable, as before). New battle steps: Ice Path 1F Skier
  -- Maria, Ice Path B1F Skier Becky, Dragon's Den B1F Dragon Tamer Darin, and
  -- gym trainers Paul (1F), Fran (2F), Cody (2F), Lola (1F). Mike is
  -- avoidable. Each step's unsure says which tiles make it forced.
  -- note: NET vs checkpoint (story_presets.lua C09_RISING): identical
  -- events/engine flags and scenes, plus three extra flags from the new forced
  -- battles: EVENT_BEAT_SKIER_MARIA, EVENT_BEAT_SKIER_BECKY,
  -- EVENT_BEAT_DRAGON_TAMER_DARIN. The gym trainers' flags are in the
  -- checkpoint already (Clair's script sets all five). DRAGONS_DEN_B1F scene
  -- goes 0 -> 1 -> 0 (no net change).
  -- note: BOULDER PUSHES are written as pairs of `go` steps: "Stand <side> of
  -- boulder N" = walk to that tile WITHOUT touching any boulder (Strength is
  -- active, so bumping one pushes it); "Push boulder N <DIR> xK" = from the
  -- stand tile walk straight in DIR until the step's x,y; the boulder moves
  -- ahead of you. A missing "Stand" step means you are already on it.
  -- Solutions come from a Sokoban search over the real collision (B1F order 3,
  -- 1, 2, 4; boulder 3 of the gym needs the flagless boulder at (8,14) pushed
  -- down first, boulder 1 needs the flagless boulder at (6,1) pushed right 3).
  -- A boulder only falls through ITS OWN hole (the stonetable checks both the
  -- warp number and the object); B1F holes: boulder 1 -> (11,2), 2 -> (4,7), 3
  -- -> (5,12), 4 -> (12,13); gym 2F: boulder 1 -> (8,3), 3 -> (8,7).
  -- note: Strength: one `use STRENGTH` per floor (YES to the prompt); it stays
  -- on until you leave the floor (wOWState is reset by HandleNewMap, not by
  -- battles). ENGINE_STRENGTH_ACTIVE (a wOWState bit) is not listed.
  -- note: Field moves: Surf/Whirlpool steps are given for the Blackthorn pond
  -- and Dragon's Den (Whirlpool (10,20) is required: without it the shrine is
  -- unreachable). Route 42 Surf on the walk back to Mahogany (re-traced from
  -- C10) is only mentioned.
  -- note: Quiz: I chose the first right answer each time (Ally, Strategy,
  -- Tough person, Love, Both); the other right answers are in each step. A
  -- wrong answer only repeats the question and sets
  -- EVENT_ANSWERED_DRAGON_MASTER_QUIZ_WRONG.
  -- note: Not listed (no net change or temporary):
  -- EVENT_TEMPORARY_UNTIL_MAP_RELOAD_* (quiz), EVENT_DRAGON_SHRINE_CLAIR /
  -- EVENT_DRAGONS_DEN_CLAIR (appear+disappear), EVENT_RIVAL_DRAGONS_DEN
  -- (already set), EVENT_MAHOGANY_MART_OWNERS (cleared again by Clair, already
  -- clear), Santos' weekday flag. Optional and left out: Dratini from the
  -- Elder, Master Ball from Elm, Lorelei, items, Kimono Girl Mina.
  -- note: Conventions used here: a `go` whose x,y is a warp tile of that map
  -- (e.g. ICE_PATH_B1F (3,15), BLACKTHORN_GYM_2F (1,7), TOHJO_FALLS (13,15))
  -- means "arrive through that warp". `use` SURF/WHIRLPOOL/WATERFALL give the
  -- water tile to face from the tile before it (named in the step's unsure).
  -- "Skirt" `go` steps are waypoints: with them, EVERY shortest path between
  -- consecutive waypoints (all tie-breaks, plain step count) stays out of the
  -- sight of the avoidable trainers; without them some shortest paths walk
  -- into one. Checked with a path search over the rendered collision.
