  ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  -- C11_CHAMPION (58 steps)
  -- note: Route on foot (no Fly): Blackthorn -> Route 45 -> Route 46 -> Route
  -- 29/46 gate -> Route 29 -> New Bark (Lyra) -> Surf to Route 27 (first step
  -- into Kanto) -> Tohjo Falls (Surf + Waterfall) -> east Route 27 (Surf
  -- twice) -> Route 26 -> League Gate -> Route 23 (8 badge checks, Surf) ->
  -- Victory Road (rival) -> Indigo Plateau -> Will, Koga, Bruno, Karen, Lance
  -- -> Hall of Fame -> credits -> Continue in New Bark (15,6).
  -- note: FORCED TRAINERS (sight-line path search, spinners treated as
  -- avoidable): Route 45 Hiker Erik (or Cooltrainer Ryan: one of the two is
  -- unavoidable, I took Erik), Route 26 Cooltrainer Beth (her after-battle
  -- script asks for her number: answer NO), Victory Road 1F Veteran Matt.
  -- Routes 46/29, west Route 27, Tohjo Falls, east Route 27, Route 23, VR
  -- 2F/3F: none. Spinners next to the path that may battle by chance:
  -- Cooltrainer Megan (Route 27 (37,6), right at the Tohjo Falls exit),
  -- Cooltrainer Joyce (Route 26 (10,56)).
  -- note: NET vs checkpoint (story_presets.lua C11_CHAMPION, including its
  -- EVENT_ROUTE_36_SUDOWOODO clear): identical events/engine flags and scenes,
  -- plus the extra flags of the new forced battles: EVENT_BEAT_HIKER_ERIK,
  -- EVENT_BEAT_COOLTRAINERF_BETH, EVENT_BETH_ASKED_FOR_PHONE_NUMBER,
  -- EVENT_BEAT_VETERANM_MATT. Phone list unchanged (NO to Beth).
  -- note: Credits: `halloffame` saves the game (SaveGameData) inside the Hall
  -- of Fame and runs Credits, then soft-resets. The robot then presses Start
  -- at the title and picks Continue; SPAWN_LANCE sends the player to
  -- NEW_BARK_TOWN (15,6). Not flags but in the save: wSpawnAfterChampion,
  -- blackout point NEW_BARK_TOWN, wHallOfFameCount +1, Elm's SS Ticket call
  -- queued.
  -- note: Conventions used here: a `go` whose x,y is a warp tile of that map
  -- (e.g. ICE_PATH_B1F (3,15), BLACKTHORN_GYM_2F (1,7), TOHJO_FALLS (13,15))
  -- means "arrive through that warp". `use` SURF/WHIRLPOOL/WATERFALL give the
  -- water tile to face from the tile before it (named in the step's unsure).
  -- "Skirt" `go` steps are waypoints: with them, EVERY shortest path between
  -- consecutive waypoints (all tie-breaks, plain step count) stays out of the
  -- sight of the avoidable trainers; without them some shortest paths walk
  -- into one. Checked with a path search over the rendered collision.
  -- note: Party levels / money as in presets/C11_CHAMPION_notes.md (Lyra
  -- LYRA1_12, rival RIVAL1_14, Will/Koga/Bruno/Karen 1, CHAMPION LANCE); the
  -- three extra forced battles add some money.
